<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">European Court of Auditors</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The European Court of Auditors is the institution that audits the finances of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>. Created by a treaty of 1975, it began work in 1977 and is based in Luxembourg. It checks that EU revenue is collected and money spent legally and soundly, and publishes an annual report on the EU budget; it became a full institution of the Union under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maastricht-treaty">Maastricht Treaty</a>, in force from 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/european-court-of-auditors.jpg" alt="European Court of Auditors" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: European Court of Auditors · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ECA-logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
